# CLI:

## DOD:

### RootModel

App's main model should hold:
- Init
- Locked status
- Server (has the socket handle & status)
- Current tab in tabs list 
- Loading status
- Log buffer (ViewPort bubble)
- Submodels

Lock is on by default. Loading is global to prevent "sending" multiple requests
too rootkit, while still handling user's input and allowing him to move between
tabs.
UI has header, tabbar submodel viewport on the left, loading, status & logs on
the right, and footer.

Init is fast but async for fullscreen apps, so use the Init flag to wait for 
BubbleTea. Set it to false when recieving 1st windowsizeupdate

Update should handle:
- Global Keybinds
- ConnectionStatusUpdate (dispatch listen job on disconnect)
- Window resize (pass it to child as well)
- Current submodel's update
- Ping backend to check if conn is still alive (fire ConnectionStatusUpdate)

### Submodels

They are like my own bubbles. Their View is rendered in the viewport part on the
right of main UI. They each correspond to one tab of the UI, thus their update
method is only called when they are in focus.
They all receive pointers to root's Loading, Server & Logs buffer(or bubble
idk).

UI bubbles used:
- Exec: ViewPort + TextInput
- Hide: Custom strings idk
- Upload: FilePicker, List
- Download: List, TextInput

Update flow:
- If disconnected, some string
- If Loading, listen for the custom Msg fired by our command & prevent Enter
- On our Msg: flip loading to false, append to global logs, update UI

